n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 17.8% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;font-weight: bold;\"> 4.1% </td>\n  </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\n`````\n:::\n:::\n\n\n<br>\n\n## Table 2. By Race/Ethnicity: Percentage of Supervision Episodes/Referrals with a Technical Violation\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {.cell-output-display}\n`````{=html}\n<table class=\"table table-striped table-hover table-condensed table-responsive\" style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\">\n <thead>\n  <tr>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Race/Ethnicity </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Youth (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Referrals (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Unique Supervision Episodes (N) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Supervision Episodes, Percent of Sample (column %) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Supervision Episodes, with at least one technical violations (row %) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Supervision Episodes, with at least one technical violations (RRI to White youth) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Supervision Episodes, with at least one new offense violation (row %) </th>\n   <th style=\"text-align:center;\"> Supervision Episodes, with at least one new offense violation (RRI to White youth) </th>\n  </tr>\n </thead>\n<tbody>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Asian </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 62 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 68 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 70 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.9% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 5.7% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.5 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.0% </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 0.0 </td>\n  </tr>\n  <tr>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> Black </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 2,962 </td>\n   <td style=\"text-align:center;\"> 3,328 </td>\n   <td style=\"t